    "md5": "95f4aa4d76d8681adb9c8e611bab8abd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1765,
    "chunk_text": "General Secretary of Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Ranjith Madduma Bandara in an interview with Daily Mirror stated that his party will be forming an alliance with UNP for upcoming elections.He stated that the government has failed to deliver on the promises given to the public and is driving the country towards a dictatorship. He further stated that the government\u2019s inability to take actions against members and associates of their party who are alleged of corruption and crimes is questionable.\n\nQ While the opposition alleges that the popularity of the government is lost, there is an equally weak opposition. Being the main opposition party, what is\u00a0your response?\n\nQ When SJB broke away from UNP and Ranil Wickremesinghe, the latter was used by Rajapakse\u2019s and made the President.\u00a0 Do you think separating from RW is a mistake?\n\nDuring 2019/2020 period party members requested to make Sajith Premadasa the Party Leader. By following that request we attempted to make Sajith Premadasa the leader of the party for the parliamentary elections in 2019. We made the request, but since there was no such opportunity we had to form Samagi Janabalawegaya under Sajith Premadasa\u2019s leadership.\n\nWe are content with our decision as SJB won 60 seats at the parliamentary elections while the UNP was able to secure only one seat. Also, we became the main opposition party. This means the decision we took was correct. Today, irrespective of the voters\u2019 strength of the UNP, the people have requested both the parties to join. We will be\u00a0forming an Alliance.\n\nQRecently we saw Ranil Wickremesinghe returning to the Opposition Head office. What was the discussion about? Was is about the alliance? Where would Ranil stand in the UNP, SJB or in the Opposition?"
