    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka seeks Interpol Red Notices for 93 suspects hiding abroad\n\nColombo, Aug. 13 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka has obtained Interpol Red Notices for 93 suspects believed to be hiding overseas in connection with crimes committed in the country, Police Spokesman ASP F.U. Wootler said today.\n\nSpeaking at a special press briefing held to brief the public on the \u201cRatama Ekata\u201d national operation, Wootler said authorities have been working to bring suspects wanted in connection with serious crimes back to Sri Lanka through international cooperation.\n\nHe said 38 suspects had been brought back to Sri Lanka through Interpol Red Notices during 2024, 2025 and the period that has elapsed this year.\n\nIn addition, another 35 notorious criminals had been brought back to the country through the direct intervention of the Inspector General of Police, he said.\n\nWootler also revealed that authorities have launched a special programme to confiscate assets allegedly acquired through illegal activities by suspects brought back to Sri Lanka.\n\nThe assets include vehicles, houses, gold and land believed to have been acquired through illicit means.\n\nAccording to the Police Spokesman, steps were taken in 2024 to freeze or otherwise immobilise assets worth approximately Rs. 1.49 billion as an initial step towards transferring them to the State.\n\nIn 2025, assets valued at approximately Rs. 1.549 billion were similarly subjected to preliminary legal measures for State acquisition."
