    "chunk_text": "Remembering Gunapala Malalasekera:  Great Intellectual who brought Sinhala and English together\n\nInspired by the Buddhist revival led by Anagarika Dharmapala, he began using the name \u2018Gunapala Piyasena\u2019 in place of his foreign names, \u2018George\u2019 and \u2018Pieris\u2019, and subsequently became known as G. P. Malalasekera\n\nIn today\u2019s world, we are unlikely to encounter another academic, scholar, and diplomat who has left such an indelible mark\u2014both internationally and within the nation\u2019s own history\u2014as Sri Lanka\u2019s Gunapala Malalasekera.\n\nindeed, he is a distinguished son of Sri Lanka who commands global renown. He left an indelible mark on the field of the English language through his English-Sinhala dictionary\u2014a legacy destined to endure for centuries. He served as Sri Lanka\u2019s first official representative in Russia, as well as High Commissioner to Canada and the United Kingdom.\n\nAdditionally, he served as Sri Lanka\u2019s Permanent Representative to the United Nations in New York, distinguishing himself as a scholarly diplomat. A statue of this peerless Sri Lankan, who rendered incomparable service to the nation, is being unveiled on August 14, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. in the historic town of Panadura \u2014 the place where he lived. It is particularly significant that this initiative of the Professor Gunapala Malalasekera Foundation has come to fruition at this juncture.\n\nHe was born on November 9, 1899, in the Malamulla area of \u200b\u200bPanadura, under the name Malalage George Peiris Malalasekera. His father was the renowned indigenous physician, Ayurvedic physician Malalage Siyadoris Peiris Malalasekera."
  },
