    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "35d257a7807df6eab7b5d96f4799fc4d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1067,
    "chunk_text": "It\u2019s time to fix the street lights\n\nStreet lights don\u2019t exist in many rural parts of the country. This concerns the safety of people who travel along these roads, especially after dark. In areas such as Medawachchiya, people are afraid to travel at night as they fear elephants roaming the area. This is the same in many other places frequented by wildlife. The safety of elderly persons, children and even pregnant women are at stake as a result of such poor infrastructure. Successive governments have ignored putting up street lights in by roads and these matters have often been overlooked. The Neluwa-Pelawatte road for instance doesn\u2019t have proper street lighting despite it being a main road. Many roads in Colombo are the same. There was a time when all street lights were operated using solar power. A Colombo mayoress even changed the light bulbs around Viharamaha Devi park. But today, most of these bulbs are defunct. Therefore,\u00a0 it is the duty of the subject minister and relevant authorities to provide a solution to the issue of street lighting."
  },
