    "chunk_size_bytes": 1430,
    "chunk_text": "Some have called the August 7 deal a \u2018Muslim NATO\u2019 because it contains an Article 5\u2011like clause warning any aggressor that an attack on one will be regarded as an attack on all. This raises serious security concerns with global implications, since all three nations face unresolved disputes \u2018 Pakistan with India and Afghanistan; Saudi Arabia with Iran, the Houthis in Yemen, and other regional rivals; and T\u00fcrkiye with Greece.\n\nSigned by T\u00fcrkiye\u2019s President Recep Tayyip Erdo\u011fan, Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, and Pakistan\u2019s Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, the Mecca agreement underscores the emerging security realities of the Middle East after Iran demonstrated its ability to withstand both the United States and Israel.\n\nThe Mecca pact also exposed the unreliability of the United States as a security partner. Saudi Arabia has bitter experience with Washington, which failed to respond to drone and cruise\u2011missile attacks on Saudi oil facilities in September, allegedly carried out by Iran. Saudi Arabia was shocked when Israel struck a residential facility housing a Hamas peace delegation in Qatar last year, with the US maintaining strategic ignorance, thus abandoning Qatar despite close defence ties. Moreover, when the Iran war broke out, Washington was unable to provide security cover to regional countries, even as it relied on bases and radar facilities in those countries to attack Iran."
  },
