    "chunk_text": "CHEC Port City Colombo Ltd., Managing Director Xiong Hongfeng said:\u00a0 \u201cAustralia represents a significant market for Sri Lanka, and this forum provides a timely platform to engage directly with investors who are well-positioned to recognise the opportunity. We look forward to sharing what Port City Colombo has to offer as part of Sri Lanka\u2019s broader investment story.\u201d\n\nSpeakers and panellists at the events include Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Central Bank Governor Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Sri Lanka High Commissioner to Australia Yasoja Gunesekara, Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Chairman Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) Director Ray Abeywardena, Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Director General Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena, Sri Lanka Consul General to Victoria, South Australia and Tasmania Pradeepa Saram, CSE CEO Rajeeva Bandaranaike, Lynear Wealth Management Co-Founder and Managing Director Dr. Naveen Gunawardane, ACP Corum Pty Ltd. Executive Director Charles Blake, Hatton National Bank PLC Managing Director and CEO Damith Pallewatte, and CHEC Port City Colombo Ltd. Deputy Managing Director Thulci Aluwihare. They will take part in a series of panel discussions and presentations focusing on Sri Lanka\u2019s economic reforms, financial stability and capital market potential.\n\nRegistered participants will get the opportunity to access to a series of sessions offering in-depth insights into Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets, economic outlook and investment opportunities. The program will also feature a high-level panel discussion, featuring leaders and market experts who will share their perspectives on macroeconomic trends, market performance, and future growth opportunities. The forum will highlight the resilience and potential of the market, showcasing recent policy reforms, improved infrastructure, and a robust ecosystem that supports sustainable investment."
