    "md5": "4fe080d98ebd27f65f47f238020b53b4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1896,
    "chunk_text": "Land mines story, a grave  affair and as plain as pikestaff\n\nThe one million mines are a success story about removing what the war left forgotten underground. The mass grave of Chemmani is a story about confronting what the war left rotting within the national conscience. Sri Lanka needs both: if it is to look back with responsibility before it can leap forward to future prosperity and peace with justice. But better not make the beautiful but asymmetrical mistake of assuming that the two are equal and opposite elements\n\nA credible and successful\u00a0Sri Lankan transitional justice process cannot be a prosecution of one side\u2019s agenda based on any group\u2019s agendas. It must be capable of confronting abuses by the State, the LTTE, and other armed actors alike \u2013 with equal fairness and fortitude\n\nIs Rosamund Pike somehow Sri Lanka\u2019s version of the late Diana Spencer, in her avatar as an angel of mercy? There are, certainly, worse things for a country such as we are still emerging from a crippling war, than having the Gone Girl turn up to help remove our landmines.\n\nThe British actress \u2013 star of the James Bond\u00a0 movie, \u2018Die Another Day\u2019; and more recently, Oscar-nominated for her role in \u2018I, Tonya\u2019 \u2013 was in Sri Lanka this week as ambassador for the Mines Advisory Group (MAG).\n\nShe visited minefields in Mannar and Mullaitivu, meeting de-miners and families affected by the war, and observing children being taught how not to step on objects by the way that could kill or main them.\n\nPike also met the Prime Minister, other relevant governmental mandarins and National Mine Action Centre officials.\n\nWhich to my mind at least raises the Saturday morning question: is Rosamund Pike the new Princess Di? (On Monday, we may grow far more serious about attendant matters!)\n\nWell, not quite. But maybe there is a more serious point behind the perhaps flippant comparison."
  },
  {
