    "chunk_size_bytes": 1809,
    "chunk_text": "Port City Colombo pitches  Sri Lanka\u2019s South Asian investment proposition in Maldives\n\nSri Lankan High Commissioner to the Maldives Mohamed Rizvi Hassen\n\nVisit Maldives Corporation Chairperson and Maldives Association of Travel and Tour Operators (MATATO) President Abdulla Ghiyas Riyaz\n\nThe Sri Lankan High Commission in the Maldives, in collaboration with CHEC Port City Colombo Ltd., hosted the Port City Colombo Investor Forum at the Barcel\u00f3 Nasandhura Mal\u00e9 on 10 August 2026, an invitation-only engagement bringing together a curated gathering of senior Maldivian business leaders, investors and developers.\n\nThe forum marked a significant step in the deepening economic relationship between Sri Lanka and the Maldives, and continues Port City Colombo\u2019s structured program of regional investor engagement following successful forums in Singapore, the UAE and Oman this year.\n\nIt offered Maldivian business and investment leaders a first-hand opportunity to learn about Port City Colombo\u2019s investment proposition, Sri Lanka\u2019s flagship 269-hectare master-planned city and Special Economic Zone, and to explore how it can serve as a practical platform for Maldivian businesses and investors seeking to expand their presence across South Asia.\n\nOpening the forum, Sri Lankan High Commissioner to the Maldives Mohamed Rizvi Hassen set the tone for a morning of substantive dialogue, reflecting on the depth and natural complementarity of the Sri Lanka\u2013Maldives bilateral relationship. He noted that Sri Lanka and the Maldives are among the Indian Ocean\u2019s closest neighbours connected by geography, culture, and longstanding people-to-people ties, and that Port City Colombo represents a tangible and timely opportunity to translate that relationship into a new dimension of economic partnership."
