    "chunk_size_bytes": 1861,
    "chunk_text": "Listening before speaking: How Social Intelligence is redefining Public Relations\n\nThe public relations landscape is undergoing a massive transformation, shifting from traditional reactive media monitoring to proactive, real-time strategic advisory. As digital footprints expand and conversations happen at lightning speed across multiple platforms, brands are increasingly vulnerable to shifting public sentiments. Organizations can no longer wait for a monthly report to understand how their audience feels about a new product, an unfolding crisis, or a macroeconomic shift. To navigate this complex environment, leading companies are turning to social intelligence.\n\nMark&Comm recently introduced Talkwalker to the Sri Lankan market, equipping businesses with the digital tools to listen, analyze, and act on these fast-paced online conversations. Beyond merely extracting data, the platform provides a foundation for human analysis, allowing strategic advisors to interpret online sentiments and protect corporate reputations before issues escalate. Mirror Business recently sat down with Anjalie Munasinghe, Manager PR & Social Intelligence at Mark&Comm to explore the mechanics of social listening, how clients can measure its return on investment, and why reputation is fast becoming an organization\u2019s most valuable asset.\n\nQ Social intelligence has become a popular term. What does it actually mean?\n\nEvery day, thousands of conversations happen online; people share opinions, review products, and react to brands in real time. Social intelligence helps organizations understand those conversations and identify what matters. It is not just about counting mentions or likes. It is about understanding why people are talking, their underlying feelings, and emerging trends to guide strategic decisions. Basically, it is about listening before speaking."
  },
