    "md5": "76f9d38fb1f08297a773cbc21f7f1121",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1611,
    "chunk_text": "Credibility: Earned through professionalism, patrol by patrol, exercise by exercise, and decision by decision.\n\nStrategic Relevance: History records navies that disappeared not because they were defeated, but because they ceased to matter.\n\nWe must embrace innovation, invest in research, and cultivate technological mastery. Artificial intelligence must sharpen decision-making, autonomous systems must extend human capability, and data must enrich professional judgement. But technology must never become a substitute for judgement itself. Technology may determine how we operate; it must never determine why we serve.\n\nI pay tribute not only to those who wear the uniform, but equally to their families. In particular, I acknowledge Madam Rajini Perera and family, whose sacrifice accompanied General Denis Perera throughout his lifetime of service. They, too, kept the watch.\n\nWe inherited this watch from generations of Sri Lankan sailors whose courage was tested by war, whose professionalism was refined by adversity, and whose devotion to duty never sought recognition. Our duty is greater than preservation; it is improvement. We must leave behind a Navy more agile, credible, innovative, respected, and strategically relevant than the one we inherited. General Deshamanya Denis Perera understood that enduring truth. His greatest legacy was not simply the institutions he established, but the spirit of stewardship he instilled within them. The true measure of leadership lies not in preserving an inheritance unchanged, but in strengthening it before faithfully passing the watch to those who follow."
