    "chunk_size_bytes": 1616,
    "chunk_text": "We inherited this watch from generations of Sri Lankan sailors whose courage was tested by war, whose professionalism was refined by adversity, and whose devotion to duty never sought recognition. Our duty is greater than preservation; it is improvement. We must leave behind a Navy more agile, credible, innovative, respected, and strategically relevant than the one we inherited. General Deshamanya Denis Perera understood that enduring truth. His greatest legacy was not simply the institutions he established, but the spirit of stewardship he instilled within them. The true measure of leadership lies not in preserving an inheritance unchanged, but in strengthening it before faithfully passing the watch to those who follow.\n\nThe watch is not ours to possess; it is ours to preserve, strengthen, and pass on. May those who come after us find that we enlarged the inheritance placed in our hands. May they discover that we left the seas safer than we found them, the Service stronger than we inherited it, and the standard of leadership higher than the one expected of us. If another generation can say that we kept the watch faithfully, no greater tribute could be paid, no finer memorial could be built, and no more enduring legacy could be left. This is \u2018Our Watch\u2019. May we be worthy of it.\n\nThe twelfth death anniversary of Deshamanya Gen. Denis Perera fell on 11 August. This is the Denis Perera Memorial Oration 2026 delivered by Vice Admiral Damian Fernando RSP, USP, rcds, MA in International Security & Strategy (UK), MSc (DS) Mgt, AFNI, JP (Whole Island), the 27th Commander of the Sri Lanka Navy."
