    "chunk_size_bytes": 1892,
    "chunk_text": "Ukraine attacks Russia with hundreds of drones in one of Kyiv\u2019s largest aerial assaults of the conflict\n\nCNN - Russia says it shot down more than 800 Ukrainian drones overnight in what appears to be among Ukraine\u2019s largest aerial attacks on Russia, with authorities reporting at least six people killed.\n\nUkraine has increasingly fired barrages of drones at targets deep inside Russia, including warehouses and industrial plants as well as refineries.\n\nRussia\u2019s state-run TASS News said it was the largest Ukrainian drone attack since the beginning of the year \u2013 with many of the drones targeting the Moscow area where many of Russia\u2019s elite reside.\n\nAir defense forces and electronic warfare units shot down and neutralized 187 drones over the Moscow region, according to its governor, Andrey Vorobiev.\n\nGeolocated video showed a huge fire at a Wildberries warehouse in the Moscow region, the Russian equivalent of Amazon. Vorobiev said no one was injured.\n\nWildberries\u2019 warehouses have been repeatedly targeted by Ukrainian drones in recent months. The company recently announced that it would build new warehousing in neighboring Kazakhstan.\n\nOne person, an 83-year-old man, was killed by a drone attack elsewhere in the region on Sunday, according to Vorobiev.\n\nDrones were intercepted over 17 regions \u2013 mainly in southern and western Russia \u2013 according to the Russian Defense ministry.\n\nFive people were killed in Rostov in southern Russia, according to the governor of that region.\n\nRussia meanwhile continues to target the Ukrainian capital Kyiv with a mix of missiles and drones.\n\nSix people were wounded by strikes early Sunday, according to Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelensky.\n\nKremenchuk and Kryvyi Rih in central Ukraine were also hit with ballistic missiles, Zelensky said. Two people were killed in Kryvyi Rih and another in Sumy in the north, Zelensky said."
