    "chunk_text": "The historic Pussellawa Rest House has undergone renovations as part of this renewed focus, while the rest houses in Belihuloya and Kithulgala are currently being reimagined to offer an elevated hospitality experience while retaining their strong connection to their respective destinations and heritage. Both properties are scheduled to reopen to the public in October 2026.\n\nBeyond its properties, CHC\u2019s six-decade journey has been shaped by generations of employees who have welcomed guests, prepared meals, maintained historic properties and shared the stories of the destinations in which the company operates. Partners, surrounding communities and generations of travellers have also played an important role in shaping CHC\u2019s journey and its place within Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality landscape.\n\nAs travellers increasingly seek authentic experiences and stronger connections with the destinations they visit, CHC is positioning its heritage as an important foundation for its next chapter. Its collection of properties offers CHC an opportunity to combine the character and history of individual destinations with the evolving expectations in modern hospitality."
