    "chunk_text": "Govt. to appoint internal interim CEO for SriLankan this week amidst restructuring drive\n\n\u200bThe government is set to appoint an internal candidate as the interim Chief Executive Officer of loss-making\u00a0 SriLankan Airlines this week on a contract basis, ensuring management continuity as the national carrier navigates a crucial restructuring phase.\n\n\u200bWhile the specific identity of the new interim chief has not been officially disclosed, Deputy Minister of Civil Aviation Janitha Kodithuwakku confirmed that the stopgap appointment will be drawn from within the organisation. This move aims to steer daily operations while the state finalises a permanent corporate model. The airline\u2019s top executive post has remained largely in an acting capacity for over a year, following two unsuccessful recruitment drives that targeted both local and foreign professionals.\n\n\u200b\u201cWe advertised for the CEO position on two occasions, opening it to both local and foreign applicants, but the interview panel concluded that none of the candidates met the required criteria or there were complications in reaching agreements,\u201d Kodithuwakku stated. \u201cInstead of getting stuck on this, we are looking to appoint an internal CEO on a contract basis this week to manage operations until this transition period ends. Once the new model is established, we plan to make a more long-term appointment.\u201d\n\n\u200bThe management transition aligns with the government\u2019s broader policy on the national carrier. Despite the airline\u2019s historic financial difficulties, state policy firmly emphasises the necessity of maintaining a national airline due to its critical role in supporting the local economy, driving the tourism sector, and serving vital national interests during emergencies."
