    "md5": "73ae454fbec0bbdc8129f72000b370a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1908,
    "chunk_text": "For the first half, profit after tax fell 25 percent year-on-year to Rs. 180.7 million, while profit before tax declined 22 percent to Rs. 362.4 million. The weaker headline result, however, masks a substantial shift in the composition of earnings away from treasury-related gains and towards banking operations.\n\nThe improvement was largely offset by the collapse in other income, which fell 89 percent to Rs. 54.7 million from Rs. 477.0 million. The bank attributed this to the high base in the previous year, when earnings benefited from substantially higher realised capital gains on financial assets and gains on assets measured at fair value through profit or loss.\n\nThe Banking segment swung to a pre-tax profit of Rs. 306.0 million from a Rs. 27.3 million loss in the corresponding period, as segment net interest income rose 42 percent to Rs. 2.05 billion. Treasury and Investments pre-tax profit, meanwhile, dropped to Rs. 56.5 million from Rs. 491.3 million.\n\nBalance-sheet growth remained strong, with net loans expanding 15 percent from December to Rs. 72.3 billion and customer deposits rising 18 percent to Rs. 77.9 billion. Total assets increased 14 percent to Rs. 104.7 billion. On a year-on-year basis, loans grew 28 percent and deposits 32 percent.\n\nDeposit growth was heavily concentrated in time deposits. Domestic-currency time deposits increased to Rs. 60.14 billion from Rs. 49.48 billion at end-2025, while savings deposits rose only modestly to Rs. 9.85 billion from Rs. 9.64 billion. That funding mix is relevant as the bank seeks to protect margins while expanding its loan book.\n\nAsset quality improved on a gross basis, with the gross Stage 3 ratio falling to 11.30 percent from 12.00 percent at end-2025. The net Stage 3 ratio, however, was virtually unchanged at 6.53 percent against 6.52 percent, while Stage 3 provision coverage declined to 42.26 percent from 45.65 percent."
