    "chunk_text": "Vietnam Airlines launches direct Colombo flights\n\nColombo, Aug. 17 (Daily Mirror) - Vietnam Airlines has launched direct flights between Ho Chi Minh City and Colombo, strengthening air connectivity between Vietnam and Sri Lanka.\n\nThe inaugural flight from Tan Son Nhat International Airport arrived at Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) on August 16 and was welcomed with an official ceremony attended by aviation, tourism and diplomatic representatives.\n\nThe new service will operate three times a week and is expected to boost tourism, support business travel and strengthen ties between the two countries.\n\nVietnam Airlines has partnered with Advantis - Aviation Services, a subsidiary of Hayleys PLC, which has served as the airline\u2019s General Sales Agent in Sri Lanka since 2019.\n\nThe direct service will also provide Sri Lankan travellers with easier access to Vietnam and onward destinations through Vietnam Airlines\u2019 international network.\n\nVietnam\u2019s Ambassador to Sri Lanka, Trinh Thi Tam, said the new route would create opportunities to expand tourism, trade, investment and people-to-people exchanges between the two countries.\n\nAdvantis Group Managing Director Ruwan Waidyaratne said the inaugural flight marked a new chapter in connectivity between Vietnam and Sri Lanka."
