    "md5": "b2d8c0277855b89b60469a3bd6f94a43",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1938,
    "chunk_text": "Yala national park to get major development boost to ease tourist congestion\n\nColombo, Aug. 17 (Daily Mirror) - A special development project is to be implemented at the Yala National Park to improve its physical and human resources while reducing congestion and improving facilities for local and foreign tourists.\n\nMinister of Environment Dr. Dammika Patabendi held a discussion yesterday (16) with officials of the Department of Wildlife Conservation on the proposed project, which aims to introduce a new physical development plan for the park in line with international standards.\n\nThe discussion was held at the Palatupana Entrance in Zone 2 of the Yala National Park.\n\nSecretary to the Ministry of Environment K.R. Uduwawala, Additional Director General of the Department of Wildlife Conservation (Operations) Manjula Amaranath, Additional Secretary of the Wildlife Division Udaya Kumara and senior ministry officials participated in the discussion.\n\nOfficials presented a physical development plan incorporating both short- and long-term objectives. The plan focuses on improving the park's infrastructure and making it more attractive, efficient and sustainable.\n\nParticular attention was given to improving parking facilities for vehicles entering the park, upgrading service centres and developing facilities that can better cater to the growing number of visitors.\n\nThe proposed improvements include the park entrance, information centre, additional ticket counters, museum, sanitary facilities, souvenir shops and accommodation facilities for park staff.\n\nThe Department of Wildlife Conservation is also focusing on filling existing vacancies and strengthening its human resources to support the implementation of the development plan.\n\nMinister Patabendi instructed officials to address the issues identified under the plan without delay and to commence the relevant projects as soon as the necessary approvals are obtained."
  },
