    "md5": "d1a8cfe5a8bdf0894f2287b96e151d83",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1788,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe wanted to do something different and give our customers the opportunity to experience different types of biryani and flavours from across the region,\u201d the Sheraton Colombo executive chef explained.\n\n\u201cOver the 10 days, we will rotate five varieties, including Lucknow, Hyderabadi, Mumbai, Donne from Karnataka and Delhi biryani.\u201d\n\n\u201cWith the Independence Day celebrations of our neighbours, Pakistan and India, also falling during this period, we thought it was a good opportunity to bring some of those traditional flavours together here in Colombo,\u201d he added.\n\nThis brings a thoughtful, timely layer to the entire experience, making it a culinary celebration of shared regional heritage.\n\nThe tasting session on a recent Friday proved that the execution easily matches the ambition. The flavours are deep, authentic and crafted with obvious expertise. Enhancing the diverse biryani offerings is an interactive live grill section featuring an array of fresh seafood and perfectly spiced kebabs, adding a dynamic and engaging element to the dinner service. Coupled with the soothing ambiance of live music, the collaboration with JW Marriott Bengaluru\u2019s chefs delivers a truly premium dining experience.\n\nFor professionals and food enthusiasts alike, this event represents a valuable opportunity to indulge in exceptional cuisine that is often hard to find at this level of authenticity. With the festival concluding on August 23, there is a limited window to savour these historic flavours.\n\n\u2018An Ode To Mughlai Heritage\u2019 is a successful exercise in bringing diverse regional cultures to the plate, proving that great food can indeed be a bridge. The diners looking to experience this culinary journey can reserve their tables by contacting the hotel: +94 77 389 4097."
