    "md5": "1366b3428aa1b9badd10a98145839f28",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "Lokka: The call  I still half-expect\n\nWhen Harry Jayawardena passed away and on the first birthday afterwards, I wrote that not a day passed without me thinking of him. I wrote that I half-expected his almost daily phone call and the inevitably stimulating and hilarious conversation that would follow with each of us addressing the other as \u2018Lokka\u2019 or, to those who are not conversant in Sinhala, \u2018Big Guy.\u2019\n\nIt\u2019s been more than a year and a half and the statement still stands true. Harry is unforgettable. But strangely, even though I did remember him, I forgot that the 17 August would have been his 84th birthday.\n\nIt was my older daughter who reminded me: \u2018it\u2019s Uncle Harry\u2019s birthday tomorrow.\u2019 That was one of several reminders for she does chide me often, as does her sister, for being negligent of parental duties. This time, it so happened that we are in two different countries. That a little girl thought it fit to remind her father about his late friend\u2019s birthday is a measure of how close he was to the family.\u00a0 It is also a measure of his sincerity as a dear friend. He cared about who his friends cared about.\n\nHarry Jayawardena left a mark. He left many marks. The signs of his being and passing don\u2019t shout out to be remembered and appreciated. He was not into anything of that kind. He simply did what he was good at. What he created with his drive, passion and skill continues to thrive. This is because foundations were important to him. He built businesses and he acquired businesses, but in both cases he was never speculative. He is known to have been a shrewd businessman, but the truth is that he was a careful man who was meticulously diligent.\n\nSuch caution he exercised in the friendships he cultivated and this is one reason why I feel privileged to have earned his trust. He stood by me through all the storms that came my way. He would criticise me and then laugh about it."
  },
