    "md5": "4fdb5075fc4e12f3515d9268f70668f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2046,
    "chunk_text": "Zambia\u2019s President Hakainde Hichilema wins second term\n\nALJAZEERA - Zambia\u2019s President Hakainde Hichilema \u2060has won re-election for \u2060a second five-year term, according to the electoral authorities, after a race marred by allegations of fraud.\n\nResults released by the election commission in the early hours of Tuesday morning showed that Hichilema received roughly 61.4 percent of valid votes, compared with \u206038 percent for his main challenger, Brian Mundubile.\n\n\u201cI therefore declare Hichilema Hakainde S to be president-elect of the Republic of Zambia this 18th day of August, 2026,\u201d commission chairperson Mwangala Zaloumis said.\n\nIt was Hichilema\u2019s seventh run for the presidency, and he was widely expected to win due to the advantages of incumbency, while it was Mundubile\u2019s first bid to become head of state.\n\nAfter his victory was announced, hundreds of Hichilema\u2019s supporters gathered in the capital, Lusaka, wearing the red colours of his United Party for National Development (UPND), singing, dancing and setting off firecrackers in celebration.\n\nHichilema, 64, issued a statement after his victory, saying he was \u201ctruly humbled by the trust you have placed in our hands\u201d. He also told those who had backed his opponents, \u201cWe hear you, and we will continue to work for you.\u201d\n\nThere was no immediate reaction from Mundubile, the opposition leader.\n\nTensions had gripped the country in recent days after a relatively quiet run-up to the August 13 vote.\n\nOn the night of the election, \u2060authorities arrested 11 people, including leading opposition figures, in a raid that involved an exchange of gunfire, while Mundubile was present.\n\nThe government said the raid targeted \u201cmilitia activity\u201d, with those arrested allegedly caught in possession of military-grade weapons meant for an armed insurrection.\n\nMundubile\u2019s National Reconciliation Party for Unity and Prosperity (NRPUP) rejected that account, saying the raid took place at their leader\u2019s home and left a member of parliament wounded by gunfire."
